  "body": "### Summary\nAs a maintainer, I want the test target to build without Swift 6 concurrency warnings too, so that a real isolation warning stands out. Follow-up of #1364 (PR #1365), whose Compile check log still shows isolation warnings in tests.\n\n### Facts (Compile check log of #1365, head 811e97d3)\n- `App/SwiftHFRTests/…/MessageTitleToneTests.swift:21-22`\n- `App/SwiftHFRTests/…/TopicRowCuesTests.swift:75`\n- other warnings raised inside `#expect` macro expansions (main actor-isolated values read from a nonisolated test).\n\n### Scope\n- List every isolation `warning:` of the test target from the CI log, fix each at its root (`@MainActor` on the suite or test that reads main-actor state, `nonisolated` on pure helpers). No `@preconcurrency`, no `nonisolated(unsafe)`, no loosened assertion.\n\n### Acceptance\n- The Compile check job log shows no isolation `warning:` in `App/SwiftHFRTests`; all tests green.\n\n---\n_Generated by [Claude Code](https://claude.ai/code)_",
